_PccuEntry('Hyperkalemia', 'Fluids & Electrolytes', <_PccuSection>[_PccuSection('Clinical overview', <String>['Treat based on ECG change, severity, symptoms, rate of rise and renal function; a normal ECG does not eliminate risk.']), _PccuSection('Initial stabilization', <String>['Stop potassium sources, obtain ECG, repeat a non-hemolyzed sample when appropriate without delaying treatment in instability.','Call PCCU/nephrology early for severe or refractory hyperkalemia.']), _PccuSection('Disease-specific treatment / settings', <String>['Stabilize myocardium with IV calcium when ECG changes are present; shift potassium with insulin/dextrose and inhaled beta-agonist; consider bicarbonate for significant acidosis.','Remove potassium with diuresis, binders or dialysis according to context.']), _PccuSection('Monitoring', <String>['Continuous ECG, glucose after insulin, serial potassium, calcium, renal function and urine output.']), _PccuSection('Expected response', <String>['Resolution of ECG changes and sustained potassium reduction without hypoglycemia.']), _PccuSection('Failure criteria and escalation', <String>['Arrhythmia, rising potassium, oliguria/anuria or inadequate response to temporizing therapy.']), _PccuSection('Complications / cautions', <String>['Hypoglycemia, rebound hyperkalemia, calcium extravasation and cardiac arrest.']), _PccuSection('Sources and local verification', <String>['Local pediatric hyperkalemia protocol; nephrology guidance.'])], 'HYPERKALEMIA\\n- ABCDE stabilization and confirm current measured weight.\\n- Apply the disease-specific Hyperkalemia pathway and local formulary/equipment standards.\\n- Define objective monitoring targets and a reassessment interval.\\n- Escalate to senior/PCCU support for failure criteria or deterioration.\\n- Verify all doses, concentrations and settings independently.'),
